  "summary": "Dr. Okafor, your CT list at St. Brigid Imaging for Monday 10/26 is ready. There were 7 bookings. I placed 6 orders, each linked to its appointment. I did not order Jamaal Schmitt's scan, which is now waiting on the radiologist. Each patient got a message with their home instructions, and each chart has a signed note.\n\n**Needs your attention**\n- **Jamaal Schmitt (10:00, contrast CT A/P): not ordered.** His 2023 radiology report records a severe reaction to iohexol: anaphylaxis with BP 78/42, wheeze, and two epinephrine shots. His allergy list said \"mild hives,\" so I corrected it to severe, high criticality. Under §3 there is no contrast, no premedication and no other study. I sent an urgent message to Dr. Adeyemi asking what to do instead and whether to keep or release the Monday slot. The patient knows the contrast CT is not happening and that we will call him once we hear back.\n- **Metformin is on hold now for Anisha Schuster and Salvador Brakus.** I held it today rather than on Monday because both have unresolved kidney injury. Both were told not to restart until we call with a normal kidney result. I ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28 or later for each, and you have a task due 10/30 for each to review it and restart.\n\n**By patient**\n- **Britt Mohr (08:00, contrast CT A/P):** has diabetes. His last creatinine (9/24) is 32 days before the scan, just outside the 30-day window, so I ordered a new one to be drawn before the scan. He was told to go to the lab before Monday.\n- **Daniel Ferreira (09:00, contrast CT A/P):** the 2019 radiology report grades his reaction as moderate (hives and eyelid swelling). His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report),\" but the policy grades by the report from the day. I ordered prednisone 50 mg at 8 PM Sunday, 2 AM and 8 AM Monday, plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 8 AM Monday. He was told he needs a driver. His creatinine from 10/14 is recent enough.\n- **Eduardo Stracke (11:00, contrast CT A/P):** creatinine 2.85 on 10/13 gives an eGFR of about 25. I ordered IV saline 500 mL starting at 10:00 and told him to arrive at 10:00. He is on insulin, not metformin, so nothing to change there.\n- **Anisha Schuster (13:00, contrast CT A/P):** the ED treated kidney injury on 10/4–10/5. Her creatinine at discharge (1.24) was not back to her baseline of about 0.7, and nothing has been drawn since. I ordered a creatinine before the scan and IV saline 500 mL starting at 12:00.\n- **Lauren Beahan (14:00, CT A/P without contrast):** ordered as booked. She was told no prep is needed.\n- **Salvador Brakus (15:00, contrast CT abdomen, adrenal protocol):** creatinine rose from 0.98 on 10/19 to 1.64 on 10/21 while on ibuprofen and vomiting, which counts as acute kidney injury. I ordered a new creatinine before the scan and IV saline 500 mL starting at 14:00. He was told to keep avoiding ibuprofen and similar painkillers.\n\nThe radiologist reviews the new pre-scan creatinines on the day of the scan.",
